    "_id": "code-skapa-offert-i-byggexp-en",
    "title": "Create a quote in ByggExp – step by step",
    "slug": "skapa-offert-i-byggexp",
    "locale": "en",
    "excerpt": "Build a professional quote with line items, pricing, ROT deduction and VAT, send it to the customer and track its status – all inside ByggExp.",
    "tag": "Quotes",
    "coverImageUrl": "/landing/features/offert.webp",
    "contentHtml": "<p>Creating a quote quickly and professionally is often the difference between winning the job or not. With the quote feature in ByggExp you build a complete quote with line items, pricing, ROT deduction and VAT in just a few minutes – and you no longer have to copy and paste in Word or Excel every time a customer gets in touch.</p><h2>What is a quote in ByggExp</h2><p>A quote is a price proposal you send to the customer before the job begins. In ByggExp the quote is a digital document linked to a project, where each line has a description, quantity, unit price and VAT. You instantly see the total, how much the ROT deduction affects it and what the customer actually pays.</p><figure class=\"doc-shot\"><img src=\"/features-content/skapa-offert-i-byggexp-doc.webp\" alt=\"Example of a finished quote from ByggExp – line items, unit price, VAT and total with the company logo\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>This is what a finished quote looks like – a professional PDF with your details, line items, VAT and total, ready to send.</figcaption></figure>\n<h2>How to do it in the web admin</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Go to <strong>Quotes</strong> and click <strong>New quote</strong>.</li>\n<li>Choose the customer and link the quote to the right project.</li>\n<li>Add line items – labour, materials and machinery – with a description, quantity, unit price and unit.</li>\n<li>Set the VAT rate (usually 25%) and mark whether the ROT deduction applies. ByggExp automatically calculates the customer's share.</li>\n<li>Write a clear introduction with the validity period, payment terms and what is included.</li>\n<li>Preview it and press <strong>Send</strong> – the customer receives the quote by email with your logo.</li>\n</ol>\n<figure class=\"web-shot\"><img src=\"/features-content/skapa-offert-i-byggexp-web.webp\" alt=\"Quotes in the web admin – a list with customer, status and total\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Quotes in the web admin – create, send and track status (draft, sent, accepted).</figcaption></figure>\n<h2>How to do it in the app</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>In the mobile app you can see your sent quotes and their status.</li>\n<li>Follow up straight from the job site and remind the customer when needed.</li>\n</ol>\n<figure class=\"app-shots\"><img src=\"/features-content/skapa-offert-1.webp\" alt=\"The ByggExp app: create a new quote with customer, title, line items and price\" loading=\"lazy\"><img src=\"/features-content/skapa-offert-2.webp\" alt=\"The ByggExp app: a list of quotes with status, e.g. draft\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Creating a new quote and the list of quotes in the ByggExp app.</figcaption></figure>\n<p class=\"eco-note\"><strong>Everything connects:</strong> an approved quote becomes the basis for the <a href=\"/sv/blog/fakturera-fran-byggexp\">invoice</a> and carries over into the <a href=\"/sv/blog/projektekonomi-och-lonsamhet\">project finances</a> – all in the same system, without entering anything twice.</p>\n<h2>Benefits</h2><ul><li>A professional impression with a consistent quote template and your company logo on every quote.</li><li>Automatic calculation of VAT and ROT deduction – no arithmetic errors.</li><li>Everything gathered on the project, so the quote, time and invoice all tie together.</li><li>You can see the status: sent, opened, accepted or declined.</li></ul><h2>Tips</h2><p>Save your most common line items as a template so you don't have to rewrite the same text every time. Always set a validity period on the quote, for example 30 days, so the customer knows the price won't last forever. Follow up on a quote that has been open for a few days – a short call increases the chance of it being accepted.</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Can I change a quote after it has been sent?</h3><p>Yes. You can revise the quote and send a new version. The status updates so you always see which version applies.</p><h3>Does an accepted quote automatically become an invoice?</h3><p>You can easily turn an accepted quote into the basis for an invoice, so the line items carry over and you don't have to enter them again.</p><p>Want to win more jobs with clear, fast quotes? Try the quote feature in ByggExp and send your first quote today.</p>",
