    "_id": "code-loneunderlag-for-byggforetag-en",
    "title": "Payroll data for construction companies — from hours to pay",
    "slug": "loneunderlag-for-byggforetag",
    "locale": "en",
    "excerpt": "Turn logged hours, shift premiums and overtime into accurate payroll data in minutes — and export it straight to your payroll system with no manual work.",
    "tag": "Payroll",
    "coverImageUrl": "/landing/features/shiftsExport.webp",
    "contentHtml": "<p>Payroll data is where many construction companies lose both time and money — hours are added up by hand, shift premiums are missed and overtime ends up in the wrong place. With ByggExp you build accurate payroll data directly from the hours already logged on site, with no notes to copy over.</p><h2>What is payroll data?</h2><p>Payroll data is the summary of each employee's worked time for a pay period — regular hours, unsociable-hours pay (shift premiums), overtime and any absence. It is the basis payroll administration uses to pay the right wage on time.</p><h2>How to do it in the web admin</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Go to <strong>Payroll</strong> and select a pay period, for example one month.</li>\n<li>The system totals hours per employee and calculates shift premiums and overtime according to your rules.</li>\n<li>Review the rows, adjust where needed and approve any exceptions.</li>\n<li>Lock the period once everything is correct so no further changes slip in.</li>\n<li>Export the data as a file to your payroll system or payroll bureau.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>How to do it in the app</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>The team clocks in and out in the app so the hours are logged automatically throughout the period.</li>\n<li>Everyone can see their own logged hours on their phone.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Benefits</h2><ul><li>No more manual totalling — fewer calculation errors and after-the-fact corrections.</li><li>Shift premiums and overtime are calculated consistently according to your rules.</li><li>Faster payroll runs and happier employees who get paid correctly.</li><li>A traceable record if a payroll figure is questioned.</li></ul><h2>Tips</h2><p>Set a fixed cut-off date for the period so everyone knows when time needs to be reported. Review exceptions continuously through the month rather than all at once — that keeps the last day calm. Reconcile your shift-premium and overtime rules against your collective agreement once and the calculations will come out right every period.</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Can I correct an hour before payroll is run?</h3><p>Yes. As long as the period is not locked you can adjust individual rows in the web admin, and the change appears in the data straight away.</p><h3>Does it work with our payroll system?</h3><p>The data is exported as a file you can hand over to your payroll system or bureau, so you avoid keying in the hours again.</p><p>Want to shorten the time from hour to pay? Gather your hours in ByggExp and turn payroll data into a few minutes' work each period.</p><p class=\"eco-note\"><strong>It all connects:</strong> payroll data is built from <a href=\"/sv/blog/automatisk-tidrapportering-och-export\">logged hours</a> from the site, and the same hours appear in your <a href=\"/sv/blog/projektekonomi-och-lonsamhet\">project finances</a> – from working time to pay in one system.</p>",
