    "_id": "code-automatisk-tidrapportering-och-export-en",
    "title": "Automatic time reporting and export of hours",
    "slug": "automatisk-tidrapportering-och-export",
    "locale": "en",
    "excerpt": "Let GPS check-in collect worked hours per project automatically and export a finished time report to payroll straight from the web.",
    "tag": "Time reporting",
    "coverImageUrl": "/landing/features/shiftsExport.webp",
    "contentHtml": "<p>With automatic time reporting you no longer have to gather hours from scraps of paper and text messages. ByggExp logs worked hours per project when your staff check in and out on their phones, and you export a finished time report when it is time to run payroll. It saves hours every month and removes the guesswork.</p><figure class=\"video-embed\" style=\"position:relative;width:100%;aspect-ratio:16/9;margin:24px 0\"><iframe src=\"https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/w5TO127GqfU\" title=\"Automatisk tidrapportering med GPS i ByggExp\" loading=\"lazy\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" allowfullscreen style=\"position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;border:0;border-radius:12px\"></iframe></figure><h2>What is automatic time reporting?</h2><p>Automatic time reporting means the hours are counted in the background instead of being written down by hand. When a carpenter checks in at the site using GPS on their phone the clock starts, and when they check out the hours are added up on the right project. Everything gathers in one place in the web admin, where you have full control.</p><h2>How to do it in the web admin</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Create the project and add the staff who will be working on it.</li>\n<li>Go to <strong>Work shifts</strong>, select the period and project and review the logged shifts.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Export</strong> to download a finished time report for payroll or invoicing.</li>\n</ol>\n<figure class=\"web-shot\"><img src=\"/features-content/automatisk-tidrapportering-och-export-web.webp\" alt=\"Hours in the web admin – planned, GPS and manual hours per employee and day\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Hours in the web admin – planned, GPS and manual hours per employee, ready to export to payroll or invoicing.</figcaption></figure>\n<h2>How to do it in the app</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>The team downloads the ByggExp app and logs in to their accounts.</li>\n<li>At the site each person checks in – the GPS position confirms they are on location and the clock starts running.</li>\n<li>At the end of the working day they check out so the shift closes and the hours are booked to the project.</li>\n</ol>\n<figure class=\"app-shots\"><img src=\"/features-content/automatisk-tidrapportering-och-export-1.webp\" alt=\"The ByggExp app: work shifts with planned, manual and GPS hours in a monthly calendar\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Work shifts in the app – planned, manual and GPS hours in the calendar, ready to total up and export.</figcaption></figure>\n<p class=\"eco-note\"><strong>Everything connects:</strong> the hours you log here are the same hours that become <a href=\"/sv/blog/loneunderlag-for-byggforetag\">payroll data</a> and <a href=\"/sv/blog/fakturera-fran-byggexp\">invoice lines</a>, and that feed into the <a href=\"/sv/blog/projektekonomi-och-lonsamhet\">project finances</a> – record once, use everywhere.</p>\n<h2>Benefits</h2><ul><li>Accurate hours with no manual work — the hours are automatically tied to the right project.</li><li>Fast export of the time report straight to payroll or a customer invoice.</li><li>GPS-confirmed attendance gives peace of mind for both you and the employee.</li><li>Full history per person and project whenever you need to follow up.</li></ul><h2>Tips</h2><ul><li>Remind the team to check out — otherwise the shift keeps running and the hours end up wrong.</li><li>Review the period the day before payroll, so you have time to correct any forgotten check-ins or check-outs.</li><li>Use the same project name in the quote and the time report to make reconciliation easier.</li></ul><h2>Related guides on time reporting</h2><ul><li><a href=\"/sv/blog/app-for-tidrapportering-bygg\">Time reporting app for construction</a> – digital time reporting from the ground up.</li><li><a href=\"/sv/blog/stampelklocka-app-gps-bygg\">Time clock app with GPS</a> – check in and out with location confirmation.</li><li><a href=\"/sv/blog/tidrapporteringssystem-bygg\">Time reporting system for construction</a> – time tracking, time reporting and time accounting in one.</li><li><a href=\"/sv/blog/tidsregistrering-app-bygg\">Time tracking app for construction</a> – accurate working hours on your phone.</li><li><a href=\"/sv/blog/mobil-tidrapportering\">Mobile time reporting</a> – report time where the work is done.</li><li><a href=\"/sv/blog/personalliggare-bygg-app\">Staff ledger app</a> – attendance in real time, ready for the tax authority.</li><li><a href=\"/sv/blog/projektuppfoljning-bygg\">Project tracking in construction</a> – follow time and margin in real time.</li><li><a href=\"/sv/blog/tidrapportering-hantverkare\">Time reporting for tradespeople</a> and <a href=\"/sv/blog/tidrapportering-entreprenad\">for contracting work</a>.</li></ul><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What happens if someone forgets to check out?</h3><p>You can see open shifts in the web admin and adjust the time manually before you export, so payroll is always correct.</p><h3>Can I export hours for a single project?</h3><p>Yes. Filter by project and period in the Hours view and export only the shifts you want to include.</p><p>Want to stop chasing paper time slips? Try ByggExp and let the hours report themselves — from check-in to finished export.</p>",
